                                    <h1>D2C Team Structure + Hiring Guide 2026-2027</h1>
                                    <p>D2C team structure is one of the most-asked + least-documented topics — how many people, which roles, when to hire, what to pay. Getting team structure right compounds; over-hiring or under-hiring kills unit economics. Here is the practical guide by revenue stage.</p>
                                    <h2>Team Structure at ₹0-30 Lakh MRR (Pre-launch to Early)</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Team size:</strong> 2-5 people total.<br><strong>Core roles:</strong> Founder + 1 marketing + 1 ops + optionally 1 tech + 1 creator/content.<br><strong>Founder wears many hats.</strong> Marketing generalist, brand strategy, hiring.<br><strong>Outsource:</strong> Accounting, HR, specialised design, complex tech.<br><strong>Salary bands (India):</strong> Marketing manager ₹6-15L, ops manager ₹5-12L, senior founder-adjacent ₹10-25L.<br><strong>Total salary budget:</strong> ₹30-70L annual + founder.</p>
                                    <h2>Team Structure at ₹30-100 Lakh MRR (Growth Stage)</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Team size:</strong> 6-15 people.<br><strong>Core roles:</strong> Founder + marketing lead + 1-2 performance marketers + creator manager + brand designer + ops manager + customer service + 1-2 tech.<br><strong>First specialist hires:</strong> Performance marketing specialist, creator manager, brand designer.<br><strong>Growing complexity:</strong> Analytics + retention + community roles emerging.<br><strong>Salary bands (India):</strong> Marketing lead ₹15-30L, performance marketer ₹8-18L, creator manager ₹6-12L, designer ₹6-15L.<br><strong>Total salary budget:</strong> ₹1-2.5 Cr annual + founder.</p>
                                    <h2>Team Structure at ₹100 Lakh - 3 Cr MRR (Scaling)</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Team size:</strong> 15-40 people.<br><strong>Core roles:</strong> Founder + Marketing head + 3-5 performance marketers (Meta + Google + creator + retention) + Brand + Design team (2-4) + Ops + Supply chain team (3-6) + Customer service (3-6) + Tech (2-5) + Analytics + Finance.<br><strong>Function heads emerging:</strong> Marketing head, Ops head, Tech head reporting to founder.<br><strong>Salary bands (India):</strong> Marketing head / VP ₹35-70L, function heads ₹25-50L, senior specialists ₹15-30L, mid-level ₹8-20L.<br><strong>Total salary budget:</strong> ₹3-8 Cr annual + founder.</p>
                                    <h2>Team Structure at ₹3-10 Cr MRR (Enterprise-adjacent)</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Team size:</strong> 40-120 people.<br><strong>Core roles:</strong> Founder / CEO + CFO + CMO + COO + CTO + function heads with teams of 5-15 each. Multiple performance marketing specialists per platform. Full brand + creative + content teams.<br><strong>C-suite emerging:</strong> Full executive team + functional leadership.<br><strong>Salary bands (India):</strong> CMO / CFO / COO ₹75L-2 Cr + ESOP. VP-level ₹50L-1 Cr. Function heads ₹30-70L.<br><strong>Total salary budget:</strong> ₹10-30 Cr annual + founder + C-suite.</p>
                                    <h2>Common D2C Hiring Mistakes</h2>
                                    <p>1. <strong>Over-hiring pre-PMF.</strong> Team costs outrun revenue growth. Wait until unit economics prove out.<br>2. <strong>Under-investing in senior marketing.</strong> Cheap marketing leads compound into strategic errors.<br>3. <strong>Missing brand + design early.</strong> Late brand investment leaves foundational brand equity on table.<br>4. <strong>Skipping analytics + BI hire.</strong> Data-driven decisions require dedicated capacity.<br>5. <strong>Hiring functional specialists before founder can manage them.</strong> Specialists without founder oversight underperform.<br>6. <strong>Not documenting culture + values early.</strong> Culture drift accelerates with growth.<br>7. <strong>Over-optimising for salary vs total comp + ESOP.</strong> ESOP + growth-story compensation retains senior talent.</p>
                                    <h2>When to Hire vs Outsource</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Always hire in-house:</strong> Founder-adjacent, brand + creative direction, marketing strategy leadership, customer service leadership, ops leadership.<br><strong>Hybrid (in-house + agency):</strong> Performance marketing (in-house strategy + agency execution), content operations, creator management.<br><strong>Usually outsource:</strong> Accounting + finance ops, HR ops, complex tech (unless tech is core), specialised design (packaging + brand identity), legal.<br><strong>Never outsource:</strong> Brand voice + strategy, customer relationships, culture + hiring decisions.</p>
                                    <h2>Founder Time Allocation Reality</h2>
                                    <p>Founder time is the scarcest resource. Ideal allocation by stage:<br><strong>Early:</strong> 40% product + 30% marketing + 20% ops + 10% team building.<br><strong>Growth:</strong> 30% marketing + 20% product + 20% team + 15% ops + 15% capital / strategic.<br><strong>Scaling:</strong> 30% team + 25% strategy + 20% marketing / brand + 15% capital + 10% ops.<br>Founders staying too operational at scaling stage becomes bottleneck.</p>

